WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.080
The pandemic is adding another&nbsp;
layer of difficulty to life in Gaza.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.240
Vaccination uptake remains sluggish among the&nbsp;
territory's 2 million inhabitants, and as DW&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.680
Middle-East correspondent Tania Kraemer reports&nbsp;
from Gaza City, COVID-19 is further straining an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:21.120
already weak health system at a time the economy&nbsp;
is struggling and people are trying to rebuild.&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.080
Here in the center of&nbsp;
Gaza-City, in Al-Wahde Street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.120
workers are still clearing the&nbsp;
rubble of a residential building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:35.440
destroyed in the conflict between Israel and Hamas&nbsp;
in May - one of the several continuing crises.&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:42.640
A few blocks away, Dr. Shadi Awad and his team&nbsp;
have been fighting the coronavirus-pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.680
at Gaza's largest hospital: Al-Shifa Hospital.
This ward is dedicated to testing and treating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.440
patients suspected of having a COVID-19&nbsp;
infection. While the number of seriously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.800
ill patients has slightly decreased in&nbsp;
recent days, infection rates remain high.&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.440
"We used to categorize these cases in people&nbsp;
who could be sent home and treated at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.360
and cases who were admitted&nbsp;
and treated in hospital:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.080
Some were sent to intensive care. We've&nbsp;
been in this latest wave of the pandemic for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:25.200
a month. It has been the biggest and most intense&nbsp;
wave since the beginning of the pandemic in Gaza."&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:36.960
The staff are exhausted, the doctor says. Over&nbsp;
1500 people have died of COVID-19 in Gaza.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.720
The pandemic has further strained an&nbsp;
already weak health system and dire economy.&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.000
The small territory, ruled&nbsp;
by the militant group Hamas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.480
has been effectively cut off by Israel&nbsp;
and Egypt for the past decade.??&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.480
Although scarce in the beginning, vaccines&nbsp;
have become increasingly available,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.040
but more people need to take them.
"Still we will work with the community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.320
and help the authorities here to spread&nbsp;
the facts and the safety of the vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:17.360
and to encourage people to get the vaccine.&nbsp;
At the moment, Gaza has reached 40 percent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:25.040
vaccination among the targeted population."
Roughly 1.2 million out of Gaza's 2 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.840
inhabitants are eligible to get a jab at&nbsp;
a vaccination center like this one.   &nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.640
Authorities have made vaccinations&nbsp;
mandatory for certain categories of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.920
people - such as those working with the&nbsp;
public. However, reactions are mixed:   &nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.720
"In Gaza, there are a lot of problems,&nbsp;
it's very crowded. There is a lot of mixing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.680
in the workplace, schools, among&nbsp;
students, even with the elderly. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.600
Our society is very closely linked&nbsp;
so vaccination is very important. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:09.200
took the first and second doses of the Sputnik&nbsp;
vaccine and now they sent us the third dose."  &nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.440
"Here, people are generally not that concerned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.000
about taking precautionary measures. They&nbsp;
don't care about Corona that much anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.280
I feel that people are just going along&nbsp;
with things, so COVID is not affecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:22.480
them like it did before.  Maybe the most&nbsp;
important thing is the economic situation." &nbsp;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.640
While the pandemic continues&nbsp;
to weigh on daily life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:44.480
it is just one of the several ongoing&nbsp;
crises people have to deal with in Gaza.

